{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DKDgGaHaF5R61Xvrrc7u4D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '将 ''capability trap'' 从 ''structural inevitability'' 弱化为 ''primary\n2\t  contributing factor alongside fine-tuning regime''。两个 failure mechanisms (degeneracy\n3\t  + LP compression) 仍完全成立——它们的证据全部来自已完成实验，不受新实验影响。调整 claims 强度：''universally fail''\n4\t  → ''predominantly fail across tested configurations''。LoRA ablation 变为 nuanced finding：''output\n5\t  convergence is driven by capability AND fine-tuning intensity, with capability as\n6\t  the dominant factor.'' 将 QE evaluation framework (Claim 2) 提升为 co-primary contribution。标题微调为\n7\t  ''Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors: Diagnosing Why...'' 强调诊断而非绝对性。目标：EMNLP Main（adjusted\n8\t  claims）或 strong Findings。'\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: fewnerd_smoke\n11\t  plan_id: exp-020\n12\t  description: Few-NERD INTRA coarse 8-type, 1-epoch LoRA fine-tune + 200-instance\n13\t    N=8 pilot. Gate for full run.\n14\t  expected_results:\n15\t    train_loss_1epoch: 0.15\n16\t    eval_loss_1epoch: 0.12\n17\t    greedy_f1_200inst: 0.78\n18\t    parse_rate: 0.998\n19\t    pilot_sj_rho_full: 0.3\n20\t    pilot_degeneracy_rate: 0.22\n21\t    pilot_oracle_f1: 0.86\n22\t    pilot_headroom_pp: 8.0\n23\t    inference_time_200inst_minutes: 12\n24\t    n_entity_types: 8\n25\t    sample_f1_pct_zero: 8.5\n26\t  result_rationale: Few-NERD INTRA coarse（8类通用实体：Person, Organization, Location, Building,\n27\t    Product, Event, Art, Other）比 SciERC 更标准化但比 CoNLL 更细粒度。1-epoch LoRA 已足够让 Qwen3-8B\n28\t    学会格式和基本类型映射（类似 SciERC ft_001 在 1 epoch 后 NER F1=0.60）。Few-NERD 训练集大（~66K samples），1\n29\t    epoch 足以收敛基本模式。Greedy F1=0.78 符合 median 范围 [0.75, 0.85] 的下半段，因为只有 1 epoch。Degeneracy\n30\t    0.22 在 pilot（200 inst）上初步可见但 CI 宽——这个 pilot 主要验证 pipeline 可行性，不做结论。\n31\t  tables:\n32\t  - name: 'Table: Few-NERD Smoke Test Summary'\n33\t    columns:\n34\t    - Metric\n35\t    - Value\n36\t    rows:\n37\t    - - Training loss (1 epoch)\n38\t      - '0.150'\n39\t    - - Greedy NER F1 (200 inst)\n40\t      - '0.780'\n41\t    - - Oracle NER F1\n42\t      - '0.860'\n43\t    - - Headroom\n44\t      - 8.0pp\n45\t    - - Parse rate\n46\t      - 99.8%\n47\t    - - Degeneracy rate (pilot)\n48\t      - 22%\n49\t    - - SJ ρ (pilot)\n50\t      - '0.30'\n51\t  figures_description:\n52\t  - 'Training loss curve: single epoch, smooth decrease from ~0.8 to 0.15'\n53\t  analysis: Smoke test PASS。模型成功学会 Few-NERD 格式和 8 类实体标注。Greedy F1=0.78 介于 SciERC（0.66）和\n54\t    CoNLL（0.91）之间，符合 Few-NERD 的中等难度定位。Degeneracy 初步估计 ~22%，低于 capability trap 线性外推的预测值（~35-40%），暗示\n55\t    median tier 的'部分确认但不完美拟合'结论。Pipeline validated，proceed to exp-021。\n56\t- name: fewnerd_full\n57\t  plan_id: exp-021\n58\t  description: Few-NERD 3-epoch LoRA + full test set N=8, 3 seeds. 5 signals + degeneracy\n59\t    + selection.\n60\t  expected_results:\n61\t    train_loss_3epoch: 0.065\n62\t    eval_loss_3epoch: 0.078\n63\t    greedy_f1: 0.812\n64\t    oracle_f1: 0.895\n65\t    oracle_headroom_pp: 8.3\n66\t    n_test_instances: 1500\n67\t    n_valid_after_gold_filter: 1380\n68\t    parse_rate: 0.999\n69\t    degeneracy_rate: 0.26\n70\t    degeneracy_rate_3seed_mean: 0.25\n71\t    degeneracy_rate_3seed_sd: 0.018\n72\t    sj_rho_full: 0.33\n73\t    fk_rho_full: 0.28\n74\t    logprob_rho_full: 0.25\n75\t    em_rho_full: 0.35\n76\t    voting_conf_rho_full: 0.36\n77\t    sj_auroc_full: 0.72\n78\t    em_auroc_full: 0.78\n79\t    voting_conf_auroc_full: 0.73\n80\t    logprob_auroc_full: 0.68\n81\t    sj_rho_cond: 0.31\n82\t    em_rho_cond: 0.38\n83\t    voting_conf_rho_cond: 0.33\n84\t    sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.32\n85\t    sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.025\n86\t    selection_f1_greedy: 0.812\n87\t    selection_f1_sj: 0.813\n88\t    selection_f1_logprob: 0.814\n89\t    selection_f1_voting_conf: 0.811\n90\t    selection_f1_random: 0.798\n91\t    selection_f1_oracle: 0.895\n92\t    selection_gap_best_minus_greedy_pp: 0.2\n93\t    selection_bootstrap_ci_95_low: -0.8\n94\t    selection_bootstrap_ci_95_high: 1.2\n95\t    selection_permutation_p: 0.42\n96\t    capability_trap_f1_vs_degeneracy_r2_with_fewnerd: 0.72\n97\t    capability_trap_monotonicity: true\n98\t    lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.038\n99\t    lp_tied_fraction: 0.31\n100\t    sample_f1_pct_zero: 6.2\n101\t  result_rationale: 3-epoch fine-tune 使 greedy F1 从 smoke 的 0.78 提升到 0.812，对应 median\n102\t    范围 [0.75,0.85] 的中部。Degeneracy rate 0.26 的关键逻辑：capability trap 预测在 F1=0.81 时 degeneracy\n103\t    应~38%（CoNLL 0.91→58%, SciERC 0.66→21% 的线性外推），但实际只有 26%。原因：(1) Few-NERD 有 8 种实体类型（vs\n104\t    CoNLL 的 4 种），类型多样性提供更多变异维度，使得即使 overall F1 高，individual spans 仍有组合空间；(2) Few-NERD\n105\t    实例更长/实体更密，per-instance 的 combinatorial space 抑制了完全 convergence。这就是 median 的核心信号：monotonicity\n106\t    成立（F1 越高 degeneracy 越高），但 R²=0.72 而非 0.95——task structure（类型数、实体密度）是 residual\n107\t    variance 的来源。Selection gap +0.2pp 的逻辑：degeneracy 26% 介于 SciERC（21%，gap≈0）和 CoNLL（58%，gap≈0）之间，bootstrap\n108\t    p=0.42 说明完全不显著。信号排序 VC>EM>SJ>FK>LP 与 CoNLL 类似但 SJ-LP gap 更小（0.08 vs SciERC 的 0.15），因为\n109\t    8 类系统的 LP 信号比 6 类科学文本更 informative。\n110\t  tables:\n111\t  - name: 'Table: Few-NERD Full Results — QE Correlation (ρ, 3-seed mean±sd)'\n112\t    columns:\n113\t    - Signal\n114\t    - NER ρ (full)\n115\t    - NER ρ (cond)\n116\t    - AUROC\n117\t    rows:\n118\t    - - Voting_conf\n119\t      - 0.360±0.022\n120\t      - 0.330±0.028\n121\t      - '0.730'\n122\t    - - EM\n123\t      - 0.350±0.019\n124\t      - 0.380±0.024\n125\t      - '0.780'\n126\t    - - SJ\n127\t      - 0.320±0.025\n128\t      - 0.310±0.030\n129\t      - '0.720'\n130\t    - - FK\n131\t      - 0.280±0.020\n132\t      - 0.260±0.025\n133\t      - '0.660'\n134\t    - - Logprob\n135\t      - 0.250±0.018\n136\t      - 0.220±0.022\n137\t      - '0.680'\n138\t  - name: 'Table: Few-NERD Selection F1 (N=8, T=1.0)'\n139\t    columns:\n140\t    - Method\n141\t    - F1\n142\t    - Δ vs greedy (pp)\n143\t    rows:\n144\t    - - Oracle\n145\t      - '0.895'\n146\t      - '+8.3'\n147\t    - - Logprob\n148\t      - '0.814'\n149\t      - '+0.2'\n150\t    - - SJ\n151\t      - '0.813'\n152\t      - '+0.1'\n153\t    - - Greedy (T=0)\n154\t      - '0.812'\n155\t      - —\n156\t    - - Voting_conf\n157\t      - '0.811'\n158\t      - '-0.1'\n159\t    - - Random\n160\t      - '0.798'\n161\t      - '-1.4'\n162\t  - name: 'Table: Capability Trap — Cross-Dataset Degeneracy'\n163\t    columns:\n164\t    - Dataset\n165\t    - Greedy F1\n166\t    - Degeneracy %\n167\t    - Predicted %\n168\t    - Residual\n169\t    rows:\n170\t    - - CoNLL-2003\n171\t      - '0.912'\n172\t      - 58%\n173\t      - —\n174\t      - —\n175\t    - - Few-NERD\n176\t      - '0.812'\n177\t      - 26%\n178\t      - 38%\n179\t      - -12pp\n180\t    - - SciERC\n181\t      - '0.663'\n182\t      - 21%\n183\t      - —\n184\t      - —\n185\t    - - WNUT-17\n186\t      - '0.523'\n187\t      - ~0%\n188\t      - —\n189\t      - —\n190\t  figures_description:\n191\t  - 'Scatter: F1 vs degeneracy rate (4 datasets). Regression line R²=0.72. Few-NERD\n192\t    sits below the line, indicating task structure modulates the capability-degeneracy\n193\t    relationship.'\n194\t  - 'Bar chart: Selection F1 across 4 datasets. All signals ≈ greedy on Few-NERD.\n195\t    Error bars (3-seed) overlap heavily.'\n196\t  analysis: Few-NERD 为 capability trap 提供 partial confirmation：degeneracy 单调性成立（F1\n197\t    越高，degeneracy 越高），但 R² 从 3-point 的 0.95+ 下降到 4-point 的 0.72。这要求将 capability trap\n198\t    从 'structural inevitability' 调整为 'primary contributing factor'，因为 task structure（类型数量、实体密度）引入了不可忽略的\n199\t    residual。Selection 结果（+0.2pp, p=0.42）处于 median 定义的模糊区间——不显著优于 greedy，但也没有像 SciERC\n200\t    那样 greedy 明确 dominate。这使得 'universally fail' 需弱化为 'predominantly fail'。QE signals\n201\t    仍然有效（SJ ρ=0.32 > LP ρ=0.25），支撑 Claim 2 的 QE framework contribution。\n202\t- name: 3rd_seed_scierc\n203\t  plan_id: exp-022\n204\t  description: SciERC NER+RE N=8, seed=789. 第3个 seed 用于 Fisher combined p-value。\n205\t  expected_results:\n206\t    ner_greedy_f1: 0.661\n207\t    ner_oracle_f1: 0.779\n208\t    ner_headroom_pp: 11.8\n209\t    ner_sj_rho_full: 0.372\n210\t    ner_fk_rho_full: 0.258\n211\t    ner_logprob_rho_full: 0.218\n212\t    ner_em_rho_full: 0.305\n213\t    ner_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.388\n214\t    ner_sj_auroc: 0.698\n215\t    ner_em_auroc: 0.755\n216\t    re_greedy_f1: 0.415\n217\t    re_oracle_f1: 0.582\n218\t    re_headroom_pp: 16.7\n219\t    re_sj_rho_full: 0.258\n220\t    re_fk_rho_full: 0.285\n221\t    re_logprob_rho_full: 0.242\n222\t    re_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.34\n223\t    re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 44.8\n224\t    re_lp_gt_sj: false\n225\t    re_sj_minus_lp_rho: 0.016\n226\t    ner_sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.381\n227\t    ner_sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.032\n228\t    re_sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.261\n229\t    re_sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.012\n230\t    re_lp_rho_3seed_mean: 0.268\n231\t    re_lp_rho_3seed_sd: 0.038\n232\t    fisher_combined_p_sj_gt_lp_ner: 0.028\n233\t    fisher_combined_p_sj_gt_lp_ner_significant: true\n234\t    fisher_combined_p_lp_gt_sj_re: 0.085\n235\t    fisher_combined_p_lp_gt_sj_re_significant: false\n236\t    selection_f1_greedy: 0.661\n237\t    selection_f1_logprob: 0.654\n238\t    selection_f1_sj: 0.651\n239\t    selection_f1_oracle: 0.779\n240\t    degeneracy_rate_ner: 0.23\n241\t    n_instances: 529\n242\t    parse_rate: 1.0\n243\t  result_rationale: 'Seed=789 的 NER 结果高度稳定（SJ ρ=0.372 vs 已有 seeds 0.383/0.384/0.360，3-seed\n244\t    SD=0.032 落入 median 范围 [0.02, 0.045]）。关键 median 特征在 RE：seed 789 上 SJ ρ=0.258 略高于\n245\t    LP ρ=0.242，打破了 seeds 42/123 上 LP>SJ 的 pattern（seed42: LP 0.267 > SJ 0.250; seed123:\n246\t    LP 0.300 > SJ 0.283）。这使得 Fisher combined p for LP>SJ on RE = 0.085（不显著）。翻转原因：RE\n247\t    的 zero-F1 rate 在不同 seeds 间波动（43-45%），seed=789 恰好有较少的 ''complete failure'' instances\n248\t    进入 high-LP bin，削弱了 LP 的 binary classification 优势。NER 上 SJ>LP 的 Fisher p=0.028\n249\t    仍然显著，支撑 ''structural signals dominate for NER'' 的结论。但 RE signal ranking 的不稳定性要求将\n250\t    ''LP>SJ for RE'' 从 ''definitive finding'' 降级为 ''tendency across most seeds''。'\n251\t  tables:\n252\t  - name: 'Table: 3-Seed SciERC NER ρ Stability'\n253\t    columns:\n254\t    - Signal\n255\t    - Seed 42\n256\t    - Seed 123\n257\t    - Seed 789\n258\t    - Mean\n259\t    - SD\n260\t    rows:\n261\t    - - SJ\n262\t      - '0.383'\n263\t      - '0.384'\n264\t      - '0.372'\n265\t      - '0.381'\n266\t      - '0.032'\n267\t    - - FK\n268\t      - '0.259'\n269\t      - '0.266'\n270\t      - '0.258'\n271\t      - '0.261'\n272\t      - '0.004'\n273\t    - - LP\n274\t      - '0.205'\n275\t      - '0.226'\n276\t      - '0.218'\n277\t      - '0.216'\n278\t      - '0.011'\n279\t    - - VC\n280\t      - '0.379'\n281\t      - '0.407'\n282\t      - '0.388'\n283\t      - '0.391'\n284\t      - '0.014'\n285\t    - - EM\n286\t      - '0.295'\n287\t      - '0.299'\n288\t      - '0.305'\n289\t      - '0.300'\n290\t      - '0.005'\n291\t  - name: 'Table: 3-Seed SciERC RE ρ — LP vs SJ Ranking'\n292\t    columns:\n293\t    - Signal\n294\t    - Seed 42\n295\t    - Seed 123\n296\t    - Seed 789\n297\t    - Mean\n298\t    - SD\n299\t    rows:\n300\t    - - LP\n301\t      - '0.267'\n302\t      - '0.300'\n303\t      - '0.242'\n304\t      - '0.270'\n305\t      - '0.029'\n306\t    - - SJ\n307\t      - '0.250'\n308\t      - '0.283'\n309\t      - '0.258'\n310\t      - '0.264'\n311\t      - '0.017'\n312\t    - - LP>SJ?\n313\t      - Yes (+0.017)\n314\t      - Yes (+0.017)\n315\t      - No (-0.016)\n316\t      - —\n317\t      - —\n318\t  - name: 'Table: Fisher Combined p-values (3 seeds)'\n319\t    columns:\n320\t    - Hypothesis\n321\t    - Fisher χ²\n322\t    - df\n323\t    - p\n324\t    - Significant?\n325\t    rows:\n326\t    - - 'NER: SJ > LP'\n327\t      - '14.2'\n328\t      - '6'\n329\t      - '0.028'\n330\t      - Yes (p<0.05)\n331\t    - - 'RE: LP > SJ'\n332\t      - '10.8'\n333\t      - '6'\n334\t      - '0.085'\n335\t      - 'No'\n336\t  figures_description:\n337\t  - 'Forest plot: per-seed ρ estimates with 95% bootstrap CI for SJ and LP, NER and\n338\t    RE separately. NER CIs non-overlapping (SJ > LP clear). RE CIs overlapping in\n339\t    seed 789.'\n340\t  analysis: 第3个 seed 确认 NER 结论完全稳定（SJ > LP, Fisher p=0.028）。RE 上 LP>SJ 的 ranking 在\n341\t    seed 789 翻转（SJ 0.258 > LP 0.242），使得 3-seed Fisher p=0.085 未达显著水平。这是 median tier\n342\t    的核心特征之一：RE signal ranking 不够 robust 以做 definitive claim。Paper 中需表述为 'LP tends\n343\t    to outperform structural signals on RE (2/3 seeds), likely due to binary dominance\n344\t    mechanism, though this advantage does not reach statistical significance across\n345\t    all random seeds (Fisher p=0.085).' Primary claims（capability trap、NER structural>surface、selection\n346\t    fails）在 3-seed 下完全稳定。\n347\t- name: lora_rank8_ablation\n348\t  plan_id: exp-023\n349\t  description: LoRA rank=8 (vs baseline rank=16) fine-tune on SciERC + N=8 inference.\n350\t    Tests fine-tuning intensity vs capability as degeneracy driver.\n351\t  expected_results:\n352\t    train_loss_5epoch: 0.095\n353\t    eval_loss_5epoch: 0.105\n354\t    ner_greedy_f1: 0.641\n355\t    ner_oracle_f1: 0.782\n356\t    ner_headroom_pp: 14.1\n357\t    degeneracy_rate_r8: 0.12\n358\t    degeneracy_rate_r16_baseline: 0.21\n359\t    degeneracy_delta_pp: 9.0\n360\t    ner_sj_rho_full: 0.365\n361\t    ner_fk_rho_full: 0.27\n362\t    ner_logprob_rho_full: 0.195\n363\t    ner_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.39\n364\t    ner_sj_auroc: 0.69\n365\t    selection_f1_greedy_r8: 0.641\n366\t    selection_f1_logprob_r8: 0.644\n367\t    selection_f1_sj_r8: 0.642\n368\t    selection_f1_oracle_r8: 0.782\n369\t    selection_gap_logprob_minus_greedy_pp: 0.3\n370\t    lp_within_instance_range_median_r8: 0.048\n371\t    lp_tied_fraction_r8: 0.14\n372\t    re_greedy_f1: 0.385\n373\t    re_oracle_f1: 0.568\n374\t    re_degeneracy_rate_r8: 0.08\n375\t    re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 48.2\n376\t    greedy_f1_delta_r8_minus_r16: -0.022\n377\t    sj_rho_delta_r8_minus_r16: 0.005\n378\t    headroom_delta_r8_minus_r16_pp: 3.0\n379\t    non_degen_selection_gap_pp: 2.1\n380\t    n_instances: 529\n381\t    parse_rate: 0.995\n382\t  result_rationale: LoRA rank=8 的参数容量是 rank=16 的一半，模型 fine-tuning 强度更低。这导致两个效果：(1)\n383\t    greedy F1 略降（0.641 vs 0.663，-2.2pp），因为模型对 SciERC schema 的记忆不如 rank=16 完整；(2) 输出多样性更高，因为\n384\t    lower-rank adaptation 保留了更多 base model 的 stochastic behavior，degeneracy 从 21%\n385\t    降到 12%（-9pp，落入 median 范围 [5,15]）。关键逻辑：如果 degeneracy 纯粹由 capability 驱动，则 F1 降低应该已经自动解释\n386\t    degeneracy 下降（按 capability trap curve：F1 从 0.66 降到 0.64 预测 degeneracy 从 21% 降到\n387\t    ~19%，仅 -2pp）。但实际下降 9pp >> 2pp 的 capability-predicted 下降，说明 fine-tuning intensity\n388\t    本身是 independent contributing factor。Median 解读：capability trap 解释了约 22% 的 degeneracy\n389\t    reduction（2/9），fine-tuning intensity 解释了剩余 78%。但 capability 仍是跨 dataset 的 primary\n390\t    driver（CoNLL 58% vs SciERC 21% 的差异远大于 rank ablation 的 9pp）。LP compression 也略微缓解（range\n391\t    median 0.048 vs 0.041），因为 lower fine-tuning 保留了更多 generation-level diversity。Selection\n392\t    仍不显著（+0.3pp），因为即使 degeneracy 降低，LP compression 仍存在。\n393\t  tables:\n394\t  - name: 'Table: LoRA Rank Ablation — Degeneracy & Performance'\n395\t    columns:\n396\t    - Metric\n397\t    - Rank=16 (baseline)\n398\t    - Rank=8\n399\t    - Δ\n400\t    rows:\n401\t    - - NER Greedy F1\n402\t      - '0.663'\n403\t      - '0.641'\n404\t      - -2.2pp\n405\t    - - NER Oracle F1\n406\t      - '0.776'\n407\t      - '0.782'\n408\t      - +0.6pp\n409\t    - - NER Headroom\n410\t      - 11.3pp\n411\t      - 14.1pp\n412\t      - +2.8pp\n413\t    - - NER Degeneracy %\n414\t      - 21%\n415\t      - 12%\n416\t      - -9pp\n417\t    - - LP range (median nats)\n418\t      - '0.041'\n419\t      - '0.048'\n420\t      - +17%\n421\t    - - LP tied fraction\n422\t      - '0.21'\n423\t      - '0.14'\n424\t      - -7pp\n425\t    - - NER SJ ρ\n426\t      - '0.383'\n427\t      - '0.365'\n428\t      - '-0.018'\n429\t    - - Best selection F1\n430\t      - 0.650 (LP)\n431\t      - 0.644 (LP)\n432\t      - -0.6pp\n433\t  - name: 'Table: Degeneracy Attribution (NER)'\n434\t    columns:\n435\t    - Driver\n436\t    - Predicted Δ degen\n437\t    - Actual Δ degen\n438\t    - Attribution %\n439\t    rows:\n440\t    - - Capability (F1 drop 0.66→0.64)\n441\t      - -2pp\n442\t      - —\n443\t      - 22%\n444\t    - - Fine-tuning intensity (rank 16→8)\n445\t      - —\n446\t      - -7pp\n447\t      - 78%\n448\t    - - Total observed\n449\t      - —\n450\t      - -9pp\n451\t      - 100%\n452\t  - name: 'Table: Non-degenerate Subset Analysis (rank=8)'\n453\t    columns:\n454\t    - Subset\n455\t    - n\n456\t    - LP selection gap\n457\t    - SJ selection gap\n458\t    rows:\n459\t    - - All instances\n460\t      - '529'\n461\t      - +0.3pp\n462\t      - +0.1pp\n463\t    - - Non-degenerate only\n464\t      - '465'\n465\t      - +2.1pp\n466\t      - +1.5pp\n467\t    - - Non-degen, rank=16 baseline\n468\t      - '418'\n469\t      - +2.9pp (p=0.01)\n470\t      - +1.8pp\n471\t  figures_description:\n472\t  - 'Paired bar chart: degeneracy rate by rank (8 vs 16) and dataset (SciERC NER,\n473\t    SciERC RE). Clear reduction at rank=8.'\n474\t  - 'Scatter: per-instance F1 variance (rank=8 vs rank=16). Rank=8 shows wider spread,\n475\t    especially in mid-F1 range.'\n476\t  analysis: LoRA rank=8 ablation 是 median tier 的 defining experiment。Degeneracy 下降\n477\t    9pp（从 21% 到 12%）中，capability drop（F1 -2.2pp）仅能解释约 2pp，剩余 7pp 必须归因于 fine-tuning\n478\t    intensity itself。这迫使论文承认 capability trap 不是 sole driver——fine-tuning regime 是\n479\t    independent contributing factor。但关键上下文是：跨 dataset 的 degeneracy variation（CoNLL\n480\t    58% vs SciERC 21% = 37pp range）远大于 rank ablation 的 9pp，所以 capability 仍是 'dominant\n481\t    factor'。Paper framing 调整为：'Output convergence is driven by model capability (primary,\n482\t    explaining cross-dataset variance) AND fine-tuning intensity (secondary, contributing\n483\t    5-15pp within-dataset). The capability trap remains the unifying explanation for\n484\t    why test-time scaling provides diminishing returns as model quality improves.'\n485\t    Selection 仍然 fails 即使 degeneracy 降低，因为 LP compression 是 independent bottleneck（不随\n486\t    LoRA rank 改变）。\n487\t- name: claim_audit\n488\t  plan_id: exp-024\n489\t  description: Cross-chapter numerical consistency audit. 检查所有定量 claims vs source\n490\t    data。\n491\t  expected_results:\n492\t    contradictions_found: 3\n493\t    contradiction_1:\n494\t      location: Discussion vs Limitations\n495\t      issue: Discussion says '+0.1pp over single-sample', Limitations says '+0.4pp\n496\t        over greedy'\n497\t      resolution: 'Both refer to different comparisons: +0.1pp = best signal vs random\n498\t        single, +0.4pp (incorrect) should be +0.6pp = LP vs greedy (from exp_016_rerun_1024).\n499\t        Standardize to LP vs greedy +0.6pp throughout.'\n500\t    contradiction_2:\n501\t      location: Abstract vs Results\n502\t      issue: Abstract claims 'AUROC up to 0.82' but Results table shows max 0.749\n503\t        (EM on NER)\n504\t      resolution: '0.82 comes from CoNLL (SJ AUROC=0.8008 in exp_002, EM AUROC=0.8156).\n505\t        Must specify which dataset in Abstract or use max across all: CoNLL EM AUROC\n506\t        0.82.'\n507\t    contradiction_3:\n508\t      location: Intro vs Section 5\n509\t      issue: Intro claims '21-58% of instances produce identical F1' — percentages\n510\t        are from 1024-token data but cited numbers use mixed sources\n511\t      resolution: 'Verify degeneracy rates from consistent 1024-token runs. SciERC\n512\t        (1024): ~21% (from exp_012_rerun_1024 tied fraction). CoNLL: derive from exp_002\n513\t        data.'\n514\t    minor_issues_found: 4\n515\t    total_resolution_time_hours: 2\n516\t  result_rationale: Numerical inconsistencies 是 paper 在多轮实验迭代中积累的必然结果。本项目经历了 512→1024\n517\t    token 数据迁移、gold-empty filtering pipeline 修正、多 seed 数值更新等，每次都有部分 claims 未同步更新。Median\n518\t    tier 假设找到 3 个显著矛盾（realistic for a ~8-page paper with dense quantitative claims）而非\n519\t    catastrophic level（>5）的问题。这些都是 presentational issues 而非 methodological problems——底层实验数据一致。\n520\t  tables:\n521\t  - name: 'Table: Claim Audit Summary'\n522\t    columns:\n523\t    - Issue Type\n524\t    - Count\n525\t    - Severity\n526\t    rows:\n527\t    - - Major numerical contradiction\n528\t      - '3'\n529\t      - Must fix before submission\n530\t    - - Minor rounding/precision inconsistency\n531\t      - '4'\n532\t      - Fix in final pass\n533\t    - - Stale reference to old experiment\n534\t      - '2'\n535\t      - Update citation\n536\t    - - Missing CI/p-value for claimed significance\n537\t      - '1'\n538\t      - Add from bootstrap data\n539\t  figures_description: []\n540\t  analysis: Audit 发现 3 个需要修正的矛盾，均为 presentation-level 问题。最关键的是 Discussion/Limitations\n541\t    中对 selection gap magnitude 的不一致引用——这在 median tier 下尤其敏感，因为 adjusted claims 要求精确措辞（'predominantly\n542\t    fail' 而非 'universally fail'）。所有矛盾均可通过引用正确的 source experiment（exp_012_rerun_1024\n543\t    为 SciERC 的 canonical source，exp_002 为 CoNLL）解决。无 methodological 问题。建议统一使用 1024-token\n544\t    pipeline 数据作为 paper 中所有 SciERC metrics 的来源。\n545\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dbb1532-cce8-453c-a0ba-ff5d2a8428c3","uuid":"8ebf32a8-7a0a-4774-be43-3ca36959386d","timestamp":"2026-05-16T10:16:34.019Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T092241/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '将 ''capability trap'' 从 ''structural inevitability'' 弱化为 ''primary\n  contributing factor alongside fine-tuning regime''。两个 failure mechanisms (degeneracy\n  + LP compression) 仍完全成立——它们的证据全部来自已完成实验，不受新实验影响。调整 claims 强度：''universally fail''\n  → ''predominantly fail across tested configurations''。LoRA ablation 变为 nuanced finding：''output\n  convergence is driven by capability AND fine-tuning intensity, with capability as\n  the dominant factor.'' 将 QE evaluation framework (Claim 2) 提升为 co-primary contribution。标题微调为\n  ''Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors: Diagnosing Why...'' 强调诊断而非绝对性。目标：EMNLP Main（adjusted\n  claims）或 strong Findings。'\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: fewnerd_smoke\n  plan_id: exp-020\n  description: Few-NERD INTRA coarse 8-type, 1-epoch LoRA fine-tune + 200-instance\n    N=8 pilot. Gate for full run.\n  expected_results:\n    train_loss_1epoch: 0.15\n    eval_loss_1epoch: 0.12\n    greedy_f1_200inst: 0.78\n    parse_rate: 0.998\n    pilot_sj_rho_full: 0.3\n    pilot_degeneracy_rate: 0.22\n    pilot_oracle_f1: 0.86\n    pilot_headroom_pp: 8.0\n    inference_time_200inst_minutes: 12\n    n_entity_types: 8\n    sample_f1_pct_zero: 8.5\n  result_rationale: Few-NERD INTRA coarse（8类通用实体：Person, Organization, Location, Building,\n    Product, Event, Art, Other）比 SciERC 更标准化但比 CoNLL 更细粒度。1-epoch LoRA 已足够让 Qwen3-8B\n    学会格式和基本类型映射（类似 SciERC ft_001 在 1 epoch 后 NER F1=0.60）。Few-NERD 训练集大（~66K samples），1\n    epoch 足以收敛基本模式。Greedy F1=0.78 符合 median 范围 [0.75, 0.85] 的下半段，因为只有 1 epoch。Degeneracy\n    0.22 在 pilot（200 inst）上初步可见但 CI 宽——这个 pilot 主要验证 pipeline 可行性，不做结论。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Few-NERD Smoke Test Summary'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    rows:\n    - - Training loss (1 epoch)\n      - '0.150'\n    - - Greedy NER F1 (200 inst)\n      - '0.780'\n    - - Oracle NER F1\n      - '0.860'\n    - - Headroom\n      - 8.0pp\n    - - Parse rate\n      - 99.8%\n    - - Degeneracy rate (pilot)\n      - 22%\n    - - SJ ρ (pilot)\n      - '0.30'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Training loss curve: single epoch, smooth decrease from ~0.8 to 0.15'\n  analysis: Smoke test PASS。模型成功学会 Few-NERD 格式和 8 类实体标注。Greedy F1=0.78 介于 SciERC（0.66）和\n    CoNLL（0.91）之间，符合 Few-NERD 的中等难度定位。Degeneracy 初步估计 ~22%，低于 capability trap 线性外推的预测值（~35-40%），暗示\n    median tier 的'部分确认但不完美拟合'结论。Pipeline validated，proceed to exp-021。\n- name: fewnerd_full\n  plan_id: exp-021\n  description: Few-NERD 3-epoch LoRA + full test set N=8, 3 seeds. 5 signals + degeneracy\n    + selection.\n  expected_results:\n    train_loss_3epoch: 0.065\n    eval_loss_3epoch: 0.078\n    greedy_f1: 0.812\n    oracle_f1: 0.895\n    oracle_headroom_pp: 8.3\n    n_test_instances: 1500\n    n_valid_after_gold_filter: 1380\n    parse_rate: 0.999\n    degeneracy_rate: 0.26\n    degeneracy_rate_3seed_mean: 0.25\n    degeneracy_rate_3seed_sd: 0.018\n    sj_rho_full: 0.33\n    fk_rho_full: 0.28\n    logprob_rho_full: 0.25\n    em_rho_full: 0.35\n    voting_conf_rho_full: 0.36\n    sj_auroc_full: 0.72\n    em_auroc_full: 0.78\n    voting_conf_auroc_full: 0.73\n    logprob_auroc_full: 0.68\n    sj_rho_cond: 0.31\n    em_rho_cond: 0.38\n    voting_conf_rho_cond: 0.33\n    sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.32\n    sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.025\n    selection_f1_greedy: 0.812\n    selection_f1_sj: 0.813\n    selection_f1_logprob: 0.814\n    selection_f1_voting_conf: 0.811\n    selection_f1_random: 0.798\n    selection_f1_oracle: 0.895\n    selection_gap_best_minus_greedy_pp: 0.2\n    selection_bootstrap_ci_95_low: -0.8\n    selection_bootstrap_ci_95_high: 1.2\n    selection_permutation_p: 0.42\n    capability_trap_f1_vs_degeneracy_r2_with_fewnerd: 0.72\n    capability_trap_monotonicity: true\n    lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.038\n    lp_tied_fraction: 0.31\n    sample_f1_pct_zero: 6.2\n  result_rationale: 3-epoch fine-tune 使 greedy F1 从 smoke 的 0.78 提升到 0.812，对应 median\n    范围 [0.75,0.85] 的中部。Degeneracy rate 0.26 的关键逻辑：capability trap 预测在 F1=0.81 时 degeneracy\n    应~38%（CoNLL 0.91→58%, SciERC 0.66→21% 的线性外推），但实际只有 26%。原因：(1) Few-NERD 有 8 种实体类型（vs\n    CoNLL 的 4 种），类型多样性提供更多变异维度，使得即使 overall F1 高，individual spans 仍有组合空间；(2) Few-NERD\n    实例更长/实体更密，per-instance 的 combinatorial space 抑制了完全 convergence。这就是 median 的核心信号：monotonicity\n    成立（F1 越高 degeneracy 越高），但 R²=0.72 而非 0.95——task structure（类型数、实体密度）是 residual\n    variance 的来源。Selection gap +0.2pp 的逻辑：degeneracy 26% 介于 SciERC（21%，gap≈0）和 CoNLL（58%，gap≈0）之间，bootstrap\n    p=0.42 说明完全不显著。信号排序 VC>EM>SJ>FK>LP 与 CoNLL 类似但 SJ-LP gap 更小（0.08 vs SciERC 的 0.15），因为\n    8 类系统的 LP 信号比 6 类科学文本更 informative。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Few-NERD Full Results — QE Correlation (ρ, 3-seed mean±sd)'\n    columns:\n    - Signal\n    - NER ρ (full)\n    - NER ρ (cond)\n    - AUROC\n    rows:\n    - - Voting_conf\n      - 0.360±0.022\n      - 0.330±0.028\n      - '0.730'\n    - - EM\n      - 0.350±0.019\n      - 0.380±0.024\n      - '0.780'\n    - - SJ\n      - 0.320±0.025\n      - 0.310±0.030\n      - '0.720'\n    - - FK\n      - 0.280±0.020\n      - 0.260±0.025\n      - '0.660'\n    - - Logprob\n      - 0.250±0.018\n      - 0.220±0.022\n      - '0.680'\n  - name: 'Table: Few-NERD Selection F1 (N=8, T=1.0)'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - F1\n    - Δ vs greedy (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Oracle\n      - '0.895'\n      - '+8.3'\n    - - Logprob\n      - '0.814'\n      - '+0.2'\n    - - SJ\n      - '0.813'\n      - '+0.1'\n    - - Greedy (T=0)\n      - '0.812'\n      - —\n    - - Voting_conf\n      - '0.811'\n      - '-0.1'\n    - - Random\n      - '0.798'\n      - '-1.4'\n  - name: 'Table: Capability Trap — Cross-Dataset Degeneracy'\n    columns:\n    - Dataset\n    - Greedy F1\n    - Degeneracy %\n    - Predicted %\n    - Residual\n    rows:\n    - - CoNLL-2003\n      - '0.912'\n      - 58%\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - Few-NERD\n      - '0.812'\n      - 26%\n      - 38%\n      - -12pp\n    - - SciERC\n      - '0.663'\n      - 21%\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - WNUT-17\n      - '0.523'\n      - ~0%\n      - —\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: F1 vs degeneracy rate (4 datasets). Regression line R²=0.72. Few-NERD\n    sits below the line, indicating task structure modulates the capability-degeneracy\n    relationship.'\n  - 'Bar chart: Selection F1 across 4 datasets. All signals ≈ greedy on Few-NERD.\n    Error bars (3-seed) overlap heavily.'\n  analysis: Few-NERD 为 capability trap 提供 partial confirmation：degeneracy 单调性成立（F1\n    越高，degeneracy 越高），但 R² 从 3-point 的 0.95+ 下降到 4-point 的 0.72。这要求将 capability trap\n    从 'structural inevitability' 调整为 'primary contributing factor'，因为 task structure（类型数量、实体密度）引入了不可忽略的\n    residual。Selection 结果（+0.2pp, p=0.42）处于 median 定义的模糊区间——不显著优于 greedy，但也没有像 SciERC\n    那样 greedy 明确 dominate。这使得 'universally fail' 需弱化为 'predominantly fail'。QE signals\n    仍然有效（SJ ρ=0.32 > LP ρ=0.25），支撑 Claim 2 的 QE framework contribution。\n- name: 3rd_seed_scierc\n  plan_id: exp-022\n  description: SciERC NER+RE N=8, seed=789. 第3个 seed 用于 Fisher combined p-value。\n  expected_results:\n    ner_greedy_f1: 0.661\n    ner_oracle_f1: 0.779\n    ner_headroom_pp: 11.8\n    ner_sj_rho_full: 0.372\n    ner_fk_rho_full: 0.258\n    ner_logprob_rho_full: 0.218\n    ner_em_rho_full: 0.305\n    ner_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.388\n    ner_sj_auroc: 0.698\n    ner_em_auroc: 0.755\n    re_greedy_f1: 0.415\n    re_oracle_f1: 0.582\n    re_headroom_pp: 16.7\n    re_sj_rho_full: 0.258\n    re_fk_rho_full: 0.285\n    re_logprob_rho_full: 0.242\n    re_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.34\n    re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 44.8\n    re_lp_gt_sj: false\n    re_sj_minus_lp_rho: 0.016\n    ner_sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.381\n    ner_sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.032\n    re_sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.261\n    re_sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.012\n    re_lp_rho_3seed_mean: 0.268\n    re_lp_rho_3seed_sd: 0.038\n    fisher_combined_p_sj_gt_lp_ner: 0.028\n    fisher_combined_p_sj_gt_lp_ner_significant: true\n    fisher_combined_p_lp_gt_sj_re: 0.085\n    fisher_combined_p_lp_gt_sj_re_significant: false\n    selection_f1_greedy: 0.661\n    selection_f1_logprob: 0.654\n    selection_f1_sj: 0.651\n    selection_f1_oracle: 0.779\n    degeneracy_rate_ner: 0.23\n    n_instances: 529\n    parse_rate: 1.0\n  result_rationale: 'Seed=789 的 NER 结果高度稳定（SJ ρ=0.372 vs 已有 seeds 0.383/0.384/0.360，3-seed\n    SD=0.032 落入 median 范围 [0.02, 0.045]）。关键 median 特征在 RE：seed 789 上 SJ ρ=0.258 略高于\n    LP ρ=0.242，打破了 seeds 42/123 上 LP>SJ 的 pattern（seed42: LP 0.267 > SJ 0.250; seed123:\n    LP 0.300 > SJ 0.283）。这使得 Fisher combined p for LP>SJ on RE = 0.085（不显著）。翻转原因：RE\n    的 zero-F1 rate 在不同 seeds 间波动（43-45%），seed=789 恰好有较少的 ''complete failure'' instances\n    进入 high-LP bin，削弱了 LP 的 binary classification 优势。NER 上 SJ>LP 的 Fisher p=0.028\n    仍然显著，支撑 ''structural signals dominate for NER'' 的结论。但 RE signal ranking 的不稳定性要求将\n    ''LP>SJ for RE'' 从 ''definitive finding'' 降级为 ''tendency across most seeds''。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 3-Seed SciERC NER ρ Stability'\n    columns:\n    - Signal\n    - Seed 42\n    - Seed 123\n    - Seed 789\n    - Mean\n    - SD\n    rows:\n    - - SJ\n      - '0.383'\n      - '0.384'\n      - '0.372'\n      - '0.381'\n      - '0.032'\n    - - FK\n      - '0.259'\n      - '0.266'\n      - '0.258'\n      - '0.261'\n      - '0.004'\n    - - LP\n      - '0.205'\n      - '0.226'\n      - '0.218'\n      - '0.216'\n      - '0.011'\n    - - VC\n      - '0.379'\n      - '0.407'\n      - '0.388'\n      - '0.391'\n      - '0.014'\n    - - EM\n      - '0.295'\n      - '0.299'\n      - '0.305'\n      - '0.300'\n      - '0.005'\n  - name: 'Table: 3-Seed SciERC RE ρ — LP vs SJ Ranking'\n    columns:\n    - Signal\n    - Seed 42\n    - Seed 123\n    - Seed 789\n    - Mean\n    - SD\n    rows:\n    - - LP\n      - '0.267'\n      - '0.300'\n      - '0.242'\n      - '0.270'\n      - '0.029'\n    - - SJ\n      - '0.250'\n      - '0.283'\n      - '0.258'\n      - '0.264'\n      - '0.017'\n    - - LP>SJ?\n      - Yes (+0.017)\n      - Yes (+0.017)\n      - No (-0.016)\n      - —\n      - —\n  - name: 'Table: Fisher Combined p-values (3 seeds)'\n    columns:\n    - Hypothesis\n    - Fisher χ²\n    - df\n    - p\n    - Significant?\n    rows:\n    - - 'NER: SJ > LP'\n      - '14.2'\n      - '6'\n      - '0.028'\n      - Yes (p<0.05)\n    - - 'RE: LP > SJ'\n      - '10.8'\n      - '6'\n      - '0.085'\n      - 'No'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: per-seed ρ estimates with 95% bootstrap CI for SJ and LP, NER and\n    RE separately. NER CIs non-overlapping (SJ > LP clear). RE CIs overlapping in\n    seed 789.'\n  analysis: 第3个 seed 确认 NER 结论完全稳定（SJ > LP, Fisher p=0.028）。RE 上 LP>SJ 的 ranking 在\n    seed 789 翻转（SJ 0.258 > LP 0.242），使得 3-seed Fisher p=0.085 未达显著水平。这是 median tier\n    的核心特征之一：RE signal ranking 不够 robust 以做 definitive claim。Paper 中需表述为 'LP tends\n    to outperform structural signals on RE (2/3 seeds), likely due to binary dominance\n    mechanism, though this advantage does not reach statistical significance across\n    all random seeds (Fisher p=0.085).' Primary claims（capability trap、NER structural>surface、selection\n    fails）在 3-seed 下完全稳定。\n- name: lora_rank8_ablation\n  plan_id: exp-023\n  description: LoRA rank=8 (vs baseline rank=16) fine-tune on SciERC + N=8 inference.\n    Tests fine-tuning intensity vs capability as degeneracy driver.\n  expected_results:\n    train_loss_5epoch: 0.095\n    eval_loss_5epoch: 0.105\n    ner_greedy_f1: 0.641\n    ner_oracle_f1: 0.782\n    ner_headroom_pp: 14.1\n    degeneracy_rate_r8: 0.12\n    degeneracy_rate_r16_baseline: 0.21\n    degeneracy_delta_pp: 9.0\n    ner_sj_rho_full: 0.365\n    ner_fk_rho_full: 0.27\n    ner_logprob_rho_full: 0.195\n    ner_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.39\n    ner_sj_auroc: 0.69\n    selection_f1_greedy_r8: 0.641\n    selection_f1_logprob_r8: 0.644\n    selection_f1_sj_r8: 0.642\n    selection_f1_oracle_r8: 0.782\n    selection_gap_logprob_minus_greedy_pp: 0.3\n    lp_within_instance_range_median_r8: 0.048\n    lp_tied_fraction_r8: 0.14\n    re_greedy_f1: 0.385\n    re_oracle_f1: 0.568\n    re_degeneracy_rate_r8: 0.08\n    re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 48.2\n    greedy_f1_delta_r8_minus_r16: -0.022\n    sj_rho_delta_r8_minus_r16: 0.005\n    headroom_delta_r8_minus_r16_pp: 3.0\n    non_degen_selection_gap_pp: 2.1\n    n_instances: 529\n    parse_rate: 0.995\n  result_rationale: LoRA rank=8 的参数容量是 rank=16 的一半，模型 fine-tuning 强度更低。这导致两个效果：(1)\n    greedy F1 略降（0.641 vs 0.663，-2.2pp），因为模型对 SciERC schema 的记忆不如 rank=16 完整；(2) 输出多样性更高，因为\n    lower-rank adaptation 保留了更多 base model 的 stochastic behavior，degeneracy 从 21%\n    降到 12%（-9pp，落入 median 范围 [5,15]）。关键逻辑：如果 degeneracy 纯粹由 capability 驱动，则 F1 降低应该已经自动解释\n    degeneracy 下降（按 capability trap curve：F1 从 0.66 降到 0.64 预测 degeneracy 从 21% 降到\n    ~19%，仅 -2pp）。但实际下降 9pp >> 2pp 的 capability-predicted 下降，说明 fine-tuning intensity\n    本身是 independent contributing factor。Median 解读：capability trap 解释了约 22% 的 degeneracy\n    reduction（2/9），fine-tuning intensity 解释了剩余 78%。但 capability 仍是跨 dataset 的 primary\n    driver（CoNLL 58% vs SciERC 21% 的差异远大于 rank ablation 的 9pp）。LP compression 也略微缓解（range\n    median 0.048 vs 0.041），因为 lower fine-tuning 保留了更多 generation-level diversity。Selection\n    仍不显著（+0.3pp），因为即使 degeneracy 降低，LP compression 仍存在。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: LoRA Rank Ablation — Degeneracy & Performance'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Rank=16 (baseline)\n    - Rank=8\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - NER Greedy F1\n      - '0.663'\n      - '0.641'\n      - -2.2pp\n    - - NER Oracle F1\n      - '0.776'\n      - '0.782'\n      - +0.6pp\n    - - NER Headroom\n      - 11.3pp\n      - 14.1pp\n      - +2.8pp\n    - - NER Degeneracy %\n      - 21%\n      - 12%\n      - -9pp\n    - - LP range (median nats)\n      - '0.041'\n      - '0.048'\n      - +17%\n    - - LP tied fraction\n      - '0.21'\n      - '0.14'\n      - -7pp\n    - - NER SJ ρ\n      - '0.383'\n      - '0.365'\n      - '-0.018'\n    - - Best selection F1\n      - 0.650 (LP)\n      - 0.644 (LP)\n      - -0.6pp\n  - name: 'Table: Degeneracy Attribution (NER)'\n    columns:\n    - Driver\n    - Predicted Δ degen\n    - Actual Δ degen\n    - Attribution %\n    rows:\n    - - Capability (F1 drop 0.66→0.64)\n      - -2pp\n      - —\n      - 22%\n    - - Fine-tuning intensity (rank 16→8)\n      - —\n      - -7pp\n      - 78%\n    - - Total observed\n      - —\n      - -9pp\n      - 100%\n  - name: 'Table: Non-degenerate Subset Analysis (rank=8)'\n    columns:\n    - Subset\n    - n\n    - LP selection gap\n    - SJ selection gap\n    rows:\n    - - All instances\n      - '529'\n      - +0.3pp\n      - +0.1pp\n    - - Non-degenerate only\n      - '465'\n      - +2.1pp\n      - +1.5pp\n    - - Non-degen, rank=16 baseline\n      - '418'\n      - +2.9pp (p=0.01)\n      - +1.8pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: degeneracy rate by rank (8 vs 16) and dataset (SciERC NER,\n    SciERC RE). Clear reduction at rank=8.'\n  - 'Scatter: per-instance F1 variance (rank=8 vs rank=16). Rank=8 shows wider spread,\n    especially in mid-F1 range.'\n  analysis: LoRA rank=8 ablation 是 median tier 的 defining experiment。Degeneracy 下降\n    9pp（从 21% 到 12%）中，capability drop（F1 -2.2pp）仅能解释约 2pp，剩余 7pp 必须归因于 fine-tuning\n    intensity itself。这迫使论文承认 capability trap 不是 sole driver——fine-tuning regime 是\n    independent contributing factor。但关键上下文是：跨 dataset 的 degeneracy variation（CoNLL\n    58% vs SciERC 21% = 37pp range）远大于 rank ablation 的 9pp，所以 capability 仍是 'dominant\n    factor'。Paper framing 调整为：'Output convergence is driven by model capability (primary,\n    explaining cross-dataset variance) AND fine-tuning intensity (secondary, contributing\n    5-15pp within-dataset). The capability trap remains the unifying explanation for\n    why test-time scaling provides diminishing returns as model quality improves.'\n    Selection 仍然 fails 即使 degeneracy 降低，因为 LP compression 是 independent bottleneck（不随\n    LoRA rank 改变）。\n- name: claim_audit\n  plan_id: exp-024\n  description: Cross-chapter numerical consistency audit. 检查所有定量 claims vs source\n    data。\n  expected_results:\n    contradictions_found: 3\n    contradiction_1:\n      location: Discussion vs Limitations\n      issue: Discussion says '+0.1pp over single-sample', Limitations says '+0.4pp\n        over greedy'\n      resolution: 'Both refer to different comparisons: +0.1pp = best signal vs random\n        single, +0.4pp (incorrect) should be +0.6pp = LP vs greedy (from exp_016_rerun_1024).\n        Standardize to LP vs greedy +0.6pp throughout.'\n    contradiction_2:\n      location: Abstract vs Results\n      issue: Abstract claims 'AUROC up to 0.82' but Results table shows max 0.749\n        (EM on NER)\n      resolution: '0.82 comes from CoNLL (SJ AUROC=0.8008 in exp_002, EM AUROC=0.8156).\n        Must specify which dataset in Abstract or use max across all: CoNLL EM AUROC\n        0.82.'\n    contradiction_3:\n      location: Intro vs Section 5\n      issue: Intro claims '21-58% of instances produce identical F1' — percentages\n        are from 1024-token data but cited numbers use mixed sources\n      resolution: 'Verify degeneracy rates from consistent 1024-token runs. SciERC\n        (1024): ~21% (from exp_012_rerun_1024 tied fraction). CoNLL: derive from exp_002\n        data.'\n    minor_issues_found: 4\n    total_resolution_time_hours: 2\n  result_rationale: Numerical inconsistencies 是 paper 在多轮实验迭代中积累的必然结果。本项目经历了 512→1024\n    token 数据迁移、gold-empty filtering pipeline 修正、多 seed 数值更新等，每次都有部分 claims 未同步更新。Median\n    tier 假设找到 3 个显著矛盾（realistic for a ~8-page paper with dense quantitative claims）而非\n    catastrophic level（>5）的问题。这些都是 presentational issues 而非 methodological problems——底层实验数据一致。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Claim Audit Summary'\n    columns:\n    - Issue Type\n    - Count\n    - Severity\n    rows:\n    - - Major numerical contradiction\n      - '3'\n      - Must fix before submission\n    - - Minor rounding/precision inconsistency\n      - '4'\n      - Fix in final pass\n    - - Stale reference to old experiment\n      - '2'\n      - Update citation\n    - - Missing CI/p-value for claimed significance\n      - '1'\n      - Add from bootstrap data\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Audit 发现 3 个需要修正的矛盾，均为 presentation-level 问题。最关键的是 Discussion/Limitations\n    中对 selection gap magnitude 的不一致引用——这在 median tier 下尤其敏感，因为 adjusted claims 要求精确措辞（'predominantly\n    fail' 而非 'universally fail'）。所有矛盾均可通过引用正确的 source experiment（exp_012_rerun_1024\n    为 SciERC 的 canonical source，exp_002 为 CoNLL）解决。无 methodological 问题。建议统一使用 1024-token\n    pipeline 数据作为 paper 中所有 SciERC metrics 的来源。\n","numLines":545,"startLine":1,"totalLines":545}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019xZZEFEZbqG4dN8Jtd1huG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2026's review process:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review Process\n\nBoth submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform, following a two-step process where authors submit articles to ARR (where submissions receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors) and then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026 (where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions).\n\n## Key Review Deadlines\n\nIf you receive review assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAfter submission, all authors must complete the author registration form by May 27, 2026 EoD AoE.\n\nThe search results indicate that EMNLP 2026 uses the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) system, and while I found information about the review process and deadlines, the specific reviewer guidelines and detailed review form questions don't appear to be prominently featured in these search results. For the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and review form specifications, you may want to check the official EMNLP 2026 website at 2026.emnlp.org or the ACL Rolling Review platform directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dbb1532-cce8-453c-a0ba-ff5d2a8428c3","uuid":"2f2273a6-1115-4f2d-9cf3-573cecefa007","timestamp":"2026-05-16T10:16:38.042Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GmCPsaanZwsh438njxHb5k","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X","url":"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2026's review process:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review Process\n\nBoth submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform, following a two-step process where authors submit articles to ARR (where submissions receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors) and then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026 (where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions).\n\n## Key Review Deadlines\n\nIf you receive review assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAfter submission, all authors must complete the author registration form by May 27, 2026 EoD AoE.\n\nThe search results indicate that EMNLP 2026 uses the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) system, and while I found information about the review process and deadlines, the specific reviewer guidelines and detailed review form questions don't appear to be prominently featured in these search results. For the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and review form specifications, you may want to check the official EMNLP 2026 website at 2026.emnlp.org or the ACL Rolling Review platform directly."],"durationSeconds":4.980558067000001}}
