in Ghahramani\\\\n    year: 2016\\\\n    venue: ICML 2016\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.02142\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: gal2016dropout\\\\n    category: ensemble_mc_dropout\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Establishes theoretical framework casting dropout as approximate Bayesian inference, enabling MC dropout for\\\\n      uncertainty estimation. Foundation for all dropout-based uncertainty methods we build upon.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  fomicheva2020unsupervised:\\\\n    title: Unsupervised Quality Estimation for Neural Machine Translation\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Marina Fomicheva\\\\n    - Shuo Sun\\\\n    - Lisa Yankovskaya\\\\n    - Frédéric Blain\\\\n    - Francisco Guzmán\\\\n    - Mark Fishel\\\\n    - Nikolaos Aletras\\\\n    - Vishrav Chaudhary\\\\n    - Lucia Specia\\\\n    year: 2020\\\\n    venue: TACL 2020\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.10608\\\\n    doi: 10.1162/tacl_a_00330\\\\n    bibtex_key: fomicheva2020unsupervised\\\\n    category: ensemble_mc_dropout\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    relevance: Applies MC dropout and ensemble-based uncertainty to NLP (MT quality estimation) without supervision, achieving\\\\n      strong correlation with human judgments. Key precedent for unsupervised uncertainty signals in NLP generation tasks.\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: paper-research:lit_batch2\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-14T18:10:52.000Z'\\\\n  cobbe2021verifiers:\\\\n    title: Training Verifiers to Solve Math Word Problems\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Karl Cobbe\\\\n    - Vineet Kosaraju\\\\n    - Mohammad Bavarian\\\\n    - Mark Chen\\\\n    - Heewoo Jun\\\\n    - Lukasz Kaiser\\\\n    - Matthias Plappert\\\\n    - Jerry Tworek\\\\n    - Jacob Hilton\\\\n    - Reiichiro Nakano\\\\n    - Christopher Hesse\\\\n