{xie2024selfevaluation} show self-evaluation improves selective generation for discrete tasks; our results suggest this does not transfer to structured extraction without learned scoring.\n26\tTrained verifiers \\cite{cobbe2021verifiers, lightman2024verify} and quality-aware decoding \\cite{fernandes2022quality} learn per-sample scoring that may bridge this gap.\n27\tConformal prediction constructs prediction sets with coverage guarantees \\cite{zhang2025conformal}; while complementary, its set-valued output differs from best-of-$N$ selection.\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012j9aktZf9LgbHXUUEJq1rH","session_id":"2dbb1532-cce8-453c-a0ba-ff5d2a8428c3","uuid":"8b98f031-7948-4b63-b4b1-10cb959c8b82","timestamp":"2026-05-16T10:18:41.437Z"}
